+**Erased by the transaction** (`UserDeletion.erased_tables/0`, the list the deleting code and the guard test share): `user_room_account_data`, `account_data`, `cross_signing_keys`, `device_keys`, `device_one_time_keys`, `device_fallback_keys`, `forgotten_rooms`, `auto_join_opt_outs`, `read_receipts`, `uia_sessions`, `oauth_account_sessions`, `oauth_consent_requests`, `oauth_codes`, `room_key_backup_sessions`, `room_key_backup_versions` (the server-side key backup of story server-side-key-backup, migration 000058: every version row, the soft-delete markers included, and every session row). `to_device_messages`, `to_device_txns` (the to-device queue and its idempotency records of story to-device-messaging, migration 000059: every message queued FOR the user, every record, and, by one more statement on `sender`, every message the user SENT that waits in another user's queue). `ToDeviceStore.send` takes its OWN fence key `to_device_erasure|<user>` (the erasure takes it exclusively inside the `sync_global` writers' lock set; it is not the `sync_global` key itself, so those writers do not make a message skip): it takes the user's lock SHARED as a try-lock (a busy lock is a 429 for the sender and a silent skip for a recipient) and refuses an erased sender with `403 M_USER_DEACTIVATED`, so a send in flight never re-creates rows after the erasure. (`oauth_codes` needs the delete policy of migration 000055.)
 
